    <string name="cannot_open_settings">Could not open accessibility settings</string>
    <string name="steps_title">Setup</string>
    <string name="steps_body">1. Enable the service in Settings → Accessibility → OpenTouchpad.\n2. If Android blocks it ("restricted setting"), open App info → ⋮ → Allow restricted settings, then try again.\n3. Come back here and adjust the size, speed and buttons to fit the user.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_title">Test checklist</string>
    <string name="tutorial_body">These screens are the ones other touchpad apps fail on (Android 16 blocks injected gestures for apps that are not declared accessibility tools):\n\n1. Permission dialog — e.g. open Telegram and tap the microphone, then use the touchpad to press "Allow".\n2. Developer options — scroll the list and toggle something.\n3. Google Play account page — scroll and tap.\n\nIf all three work, the touchpad is doing what it is meant to do.</string>

